# Component Composition Rules

## Hard Thresholds

| Rule | Limit | When exceeded |
|------|-------|---------------|
| `useState` hooks per component | ≤ 8 | Extract to custom hook in `web/src/hooks/` |
| Lines of code per `.tsx` file | ≤ 300 | Split into sub-components |
| Form field `useState` | ≤ 4 | Use `useFormReducer` |

## Required Shared Hooks

Check `web/src/hooks/README.md` BEFORE creating a new state pattern.

| Hook | File | When to use |
|------|------|------------|
| `useAsyncState<T>` | `use-async-state.ts` | Any loading/error/data triplet |
| `useFormReducer<T>` | `use-form-reducer.ts` | 5–8 form fields |
| `useTableFilters<T>` | `use-table-filters.ts` | Filter/sort/paginate collections |
| `useModal<T>` | `use-modal.ts` | Any open/close/data modal pattern |

## Form State Decision Tree

```
1–4 fields  → useState
5–8 fields  → useFormReducer (web/src/hooks/use-form-reducer.ts)
>8 fields   → React Hook Form + Zod
```

## Error UI Requirement

Every `catch` in a component **must** render `<ErrorDisplay />`. No silent failures.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT
} catch (err) {
  setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Unknown error')
}
// ...
{error && <ErrorDisplay message={error} onRetry={refetch} />}

// ❌ WRONG — user sees nothing
} catch (err) {
  console.error(err)
}
```

## Tailwind DRY Rule

Extract repeated class combinations to `@layer components` in `web/src/index.css`
after they appear in **3+ places**.

## Type Assertion Discipline

- Prefer type narrowing over `as` assertions
- `as` requires a `// SAFETY: <reason>` comment on the same line
- Never write `as unknown as T`
- Use `unknown` + type guards for external data (API responses, localStorage)

## Hook Index Requirement

Keep `web/src/hooks/README.md` current. Add a row for every hook added, renamed, or removed.

## Pre-Commit Checklist for .tsx Files

Before committing any `.tsx` file:

- [ ] ≤ 8 `useState` calls (grep to verify)
- [ ] ≤ 300 lines
- [ ] No form with > 4 field `useState` — use `useFormReducer`
- [ ] Every `catch` renders `<ErrorDisplay />`
- [ ] No `any` types
- [ ] All `as` assertions have `// SAFETY:` comment
- [ ] Shared hooks used where applicable (check `web/src/hooks/README.md`)
- [ ] Repeated Tailwind classes extracted if 3+ occurrences
- [ ] Explicit return type on all async functions
- [ ] No hardcoded strings that belong in `web/src/types.ts`
